{"id": "EUVD-2026-106891", "enisaUuid": "b8f655e4-b789-3364-b41f-4c3278cf8b90", "description": "Trigger.dev before 4.5.4 contains a hardcoded default secret vulnerability in the /coordinator Socket.IO namespace that allows unauthenticated attackers to connect using the published coordinator-secret value. Attackers can emit READY_FOR_EXECUTION to retrieve decrypted run environment variables or send TASK_RUN_FAILED_TO_RUN and similar events to tamper with arbitrary runs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:54", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/triggerdotdev/trigger.dev/security/advisories/GHSA-gg6r-gp4c-89hp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trigger-dev-before-4.5.4-hardcoded-coordinator-secret-authentication-bypass-via-socket-io"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j3cj-67wq-q96g", "CVE-2026-114088"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3452437c-5507-31d1-b601-26b10116f565", "product": {"name": "trigger.dev", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.5.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e7499b4c-8472-367d-ad32-395d144c60bc", "vendor": {"name": "triggerdotdev"}}], "isExploited": false}